I like this suggestion: it's simple to implement and for
players to understand.

There's a couple ways that could be done -- either you ask the
player rne(10) times for a monster to genocide, or you ask
them for a class and then genocide rne(10) randomly chosen
members of the class.  The first is simpler (and more helpful
to the player), although the second has some merit -- for
instance, it means you could use your uncursed scroll to
genocide arch-liches, or use a blessed scroll to target 'L'
and possibly genocide more liches, but run the chance that the
nastier ones would still be alive.  That makes it so that
both uncursed and blessed scrolls are useful in some
circumstances.

I do think that perhaps rne(10) is perhaps too steep a curve;
with only a 10% chance of genociding more than one monster,
there's not a whole lot of value to blessing your scrolls.  At
least, I'd consider it more trouble than it was worth if I
didn't have extra holy water on hand.

